comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T21:36:43.602Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for comments-audit limit semantics found closed implementation item pm-w1j3 and broad output-contract item pm-srns,but no active issue for the live package help/runtime contradiction. Reproduced during the full 6,546-comment-row audit."
  "2026-07-28T03:16:20.391Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-07-28: implementing independent scan and row-output budgets with compatibility recovery in the same managed SDK/package contract tranche; only this exact bundle is in progress."
  "2026-07-28T04:14:12.443Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: comments-audit now separates --limit-items scanning from the global --limit-rows export budget, retains --limit as a deprecated row alias with a targeted conflict error, and reports emitted versus total rows plus truncation. Unit/runtime/release-contract tests passed; a packed installed governance package proved two scanned items, two emitted rows, three total rows, and truncation without exposing temporary data."
  "2026-07-28T04:23:34.410Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/788 at initial implementation head 452f21fa1. The PR description links this canonical item and records the full local gate and packed-consumer evidence."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T04:14:13.485Z","harness:codex","Pagination semantics need named units. Item caps and row caps must be parsed independently, applied at their respective layers, and reported with both emitted and total counts so agents can distinguish bounded context from missing data."
